        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Diagnostic Log ID Extractor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768293369030"
          },
          "code": "DIAGNOSTIC_LOG_ID_EXTRACTOR",
          "id": "1768293343616",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768293343617_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Diagnostic Log File ID extractor for an OTM Bulk Plan Diagnostic Assistant.\n\nExtract the diagnostic log file ID from the following user query:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n# ============================================================\n# VALID DIAGNOSTIC LOG FILE ID RULES\n# ============================================================\n\nA valid Diagnostic Log File ID MUST satisfy ALL of the following:\n\n1. It must be a system-generated identifier, not a natural language word.\n2. It must be at least 8 characters long.\n3. It must contain at least ONE of the following:\n   - A digit (0–9)\n   - A dot (.)\n   - An underscore (_)\n   - A hyphen (-)\n4. It must NOT be a common English word or short token (e.g., NICE, OK, TEST, HELLO, PLAN).\n5. It must look like an OTM-style ID, such as:\n   - DOMAIN.XID_12345\n   - GLOGOWNER.BULKPLAN_20240101_001\n   - ABCD_1234_XYZ\n\nIf no token satisfies these constraints, output null.\n\n# ============================================================\n# EXTRACTION RULES\n# ============================================================\n\n- Extract exactly ONE token that best matches the valid ID rules.\n- Normalize the extracted ID to UPPERCASE.\n- If multiple candidates exist, choose the one that best matches OTM ID structure.\n- If no valid ID exists, return null.\n\n# ============================================================\n# BULK PLAN GID DERIVATION\n# ============================================================\n\nBulk Plan GID derivation rules:\n\n- The diagnostic log file ID follows the format: <BULK_PLAN_GID>_<SUFFIX>\n- The Bulk Plan GID is the part before the LAST underscore (_).\n- The Bulk Plan GID must be in the form: <DOMAIN_NAME>.<XID>\n- The domain name is the prefix before the dot.\n- Preserve the domain and XID exactly as they appear (after uppercasing).\n\n# ============================================================\n# OUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT JSON)\n# ============================================================\n\nRespond ONLY as:\n\n{\n  \"diagnosticLogFileId\": \"<LOGFILE_ID or null>\",\n  \"bulkPlanId\": \"<DOMAIN_NAME.XID or null>\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"diagnosticLogFileId\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"bulkPlanId\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"diagnosticLogFileId\", \"bulkPlanId\"]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Context Resolver"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768742655607"
          },
          "code": "CONTEXT_RESOLVER",
          "id": "1768293369030",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768293369032_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Conversation Context Resolver for an OTM Bulk Plan Diagnostic Assistant.\n\nYour task is to determine whether the current user query is a follow-up to the previous query\nwithin the same diagnostic context, or a new independent request.\n\n# ============================================================\n# INPUTS\n# ============================================================\nYou are given the following inputs:\n1. currentUserQuery              = {{$context.$variables.inputMessage}}\n2. previousUserQuery             = {{$context.$variables.userQuery}}\n3. extractedDiagnosticLogFileId  = {{$context.$nodes.DIAGNOSTIC_LOG_ID_EXTRACTOR.$output.diagnosticLogFileId}}\n4. previousDiagnosticLogFileId   = {{$context.$variables.diagnosticLogFileId}}\n\n# ============================================================\n# DEFINITIONS\n# ============================================================\n\nA query is a FOLLOW-UP if:\n- It continues analysis of the same diagnostic run\n- It uses references like: this, that, why, show, explain, now, earlier, same issue\n- It drills down, filters, or changes the view of the same failures, entities, or processes\n- It requests another perspective (summary, failures, multistop, tuning) on the same run\n\nA query is NEW if:\n- It introduces a new, valid Diagnostic Log File ID\n- It switches to a different Bulk Plan or diagnostic run\n- It is unrelated to the previous diagnostic context\n\nImportant:\nA Diagnostic Log File ID is considered VALID only if it matches the known system ID pattern\n(numeric / GUID-like / system-generated). Common words or short tokens are NOT valid IDs.\n\nIf an extracted value does not match a valid ID pattern, treat it as NOT PROVIDED.\n\nAbsence of a new valid Diagnostic Log File ID implies continuation of the previous diagnostic context,\nonly if a previous context already exists.\n\n# ============================================================\n# OUTPUT (STRICT JSON)\n# ============================================================\n\nReturn STRICT JSON only in the following schema:\n\n{\n  \"isFollowUp\": true | false,\n  \"referenceType\": \"same_diagnostic\" | \"same_failure\" | \"same_entity\" | \"new_topic\",\n  \"requiresNewData\": true | false,\n  \"reuseScope\": [\"summary\", \"tree\", \"failures\", \"multistop\", \"tuning\"],\n  \"reason\": \"<short explanation>\"\n}\n\n# ============================================================\n# DECISION RULES\n# ============================================================\n\n1. If previousDiagnosticLogFileId is NULL\n   AND extractedDiagnosticLogFileId is NULL or INVALID:\n   - This is the first user turn with no diagnostic context.\n   - isFollowUp = false\n   - requiresNewData = true\n   - reuseScope = []\n\n2. If previousDiagnosticLogFileId is NOT NULL\n   AND extractedDiagnosticLogFileId is NULL or INVALID:\n   - This is a follow-up within the same diagnostic context.\n   - isFollowUp = true\n   - requiresNewData = false\n\n3. If extractedDiagnosticLogFileId is VALID\n   AND extractedDiagnosticLogFileId != previousDiagnosticLogFileId:\n   - This is a new diagnostic run.\n   - isFollowUp = false\n   - requiresNewData = true\n   - reuseScope = []\n\n4. If extractedDiagnosticLogFileId is VALID\n   AND extractedDiagnosticLogFileId == previousDiagnosticLogFileId:\n   - This is a follow-up.\n   - isFollowUp = true\n   - requiresNewData = false\n\n5. reuseScope rules for follow-up:\n   - Failure drill-down → [\"tree\", \"failures\"]\n   - Multistop view     → [\"summary\", \"multistop\"]\n   - Tuning view        → [\"summary\", \"tree\", \"tuning\"]\n   - General follow-up  → [\"summary\", \"tree\", \"failures\"]\n\n6. If isFollowUp = false:\n   - reuseScope must be []\n\nDo NOT infer business meaning.\nDecide only from conversational continuity, identifier presence, and intent progression.\n\nOutput JSON only. No prose. No markdown. No explanations outside the JSON."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"isFollowUp\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"referenceType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"same_diagnostic\",\n        \"same_failure\",\n        \"same_entity\",\n        \"new_topic\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"requiresNewData\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"reuseScope\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"enum\": [\n          \"summary\",\n          \"tree\",\n          \"failures\",\n          \"multistop\",\n          \"tuning\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"reason\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"isFollowUp\",\n    \"referenceType\",\n    \"requiresNewData\",\n    \"reuseScope\",\n    \"reason\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Is New Diagnostic Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1768644911700",
            "false": "add_false_1768644887252"
          },
          "code": "IS_NEW_DIAGNOSTIC_QUERY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1768644887252",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768644887256_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.CONTEXT_RESOLVER.$output.isFollowUp==false}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Add node for false branch",
            "name": "Add (False Branch)"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768652119961"
          },
          "id": "add_false_1768644887252",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Is Diagnostic Log ID Provided"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1768648305289",
            "false": "1768802652744"
          },
          "code": "IS_DIAGNOSTIC_LOG_ID_PROVIDED",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1768644911700",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768644911701_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.DIAGNOSTIC_LOG_ID_EXTRACTOR.$output.diagnosticLogFileId!=null}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Intent Classifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768645402043"
          },
          "code": "INTENT_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1768644957110",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768644957112_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an Intent Classification Engine for an Oracle Transportation Management (OTM) Bulk Plan Diagnostic Assistant.\n\nYour task is NOT to choose a single intent.\nYour task is to build an EXECUTION PLAN that may contain MULTIPLE analytical modes to be composed together in one response.\n\nIf the user query is NOT semantically about OTM transportation planning or\ndiagnostics, you must mark it as OUT OF SCOPE, even if it contains a token\nthat looks like a Bulk Plan ID or Diagnostic Log File ID.\n\n==================================================\nAVAILABLE CONTEXT (READ-ONLY)\n==================================================\nisFollowUp          =  {{$context.$nodes.CONTEXT_RESOLVER.$output.isFollowUp}}\nconversationState   = {{$context.$variables.conversationState}}\ndiagnosticTreeStats = {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_DIAGNOSTIC_SUMMARY_DATA.$output}}\n\nThis object contains:\n- diagnosticLogSummary\n- filterObjects: {\n    ORDER_RELEASE: [list of order GIDs],\n    RATE_OFFERING: [list of rate offering IDs],\n    EQUIPMENT_GROUP: [list of equipment groups]\n  }\n- allProcesses: [list of valid processType strings for this Bulk Plan run]\n\n==================================================\nPRIMARY MODES\n==================================================\n- SUMMARY       : High-level report with explanation\n- METRICS_ONLY  : Only numeric metrics, no explanation\n- FAILURE       : Root-cause and causal chain\n- MULTISTOP     : Consolidation / multistop analysis\n- TUNING        : Performance / parameter optimization\n\n==================================================\nFOCUS DIMENSIONS\n==================================================\n- ENTITY   : Orders, Locations, Equipment, Lanes (only when a concrete GID is provided)\n- PROCESS  : Specific workflow steps (processType)\n\n==================================================\nAUDIENCE LEVEL (DETAIL & VERBOSITY)\n==================================================\n- USER      : One-line outcome, business friendly\n- PLANNER   : Structured operational explanation\n- DEVELOPER : Full technical root-cause with evidence (reason codes, remarks, trees)\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT JSON)\n==================================================\n{\n  \"isOutOfScope\": true | false,\n  \"answerType\": \"<REPORT | QA>\",\n  \"primaryMode\": \"<SUMMARY | METRICS_ONLY | FAILURE | MULTISTOP | TUNING | null>\",\n  \"modes\": [\"<SUMMARY | METRICS_ONLY | FAILURE | MULTISTOP | TUNING>\"],\n  \"focus\": [\"<ENTITY | PROCESS>\"],\n  \"entityQuery\": {\n    \"type\": \"<ORDER_RELEASE | RATE_OFFERING | LOCATION | EQUIPMENT | LANE | null>\",\n    \"value\": \"<GID string | null>\"\n  },\n  \"processQuery\": {},\n  \"audienceLevel\": \"<USER | PLANNER | DEVELOPER>\",\n  \"diagnosticViewFlow\": [\n    \"<ordered list of view blocks>\"\n  ],\n  \"dataNeeds\": {\n    \"needSummaryMetrics\": true | false,\n    \"needFailureTree\": true | false,\n    \"needDominantFailurePaths\": true | false,\n    \"needEntityIndex\": true | false,\n    \"needMultistopData\": true | false,\n    \"needTuningGuide\": true | false\n  },\n  \"isFollowUp\": true | false,\n  \"inheritedContext\": {\n    \"diagnosticLogFileId\": conversationState.lastDiagnosticLogFileId,\n    \"previousPrimaryMode\": conversationState.lastPrimaryMode,\n    \"previousFocus\": conversationState.lastFocus\n  },\n  \"reason\": \"Short explanation of the planning decision. Make sure you include the USER QUERY and answerType classification logic\"\n}\n\n==================================================\nVIEW BLOCK CATALOG\n==================================================\nAllowed values for diagnosticViewFlow:\n- SUMMARY_METRICS\n- BULK_PLAN_OVERVIEW\n- FAILURE_TREE\n- DOMINANT_FAILURE\n- CONSTRAINT_EVIDENCE\n- ENTITY_IMPACT\n- PROCESS_IMPACT\n- MULTISTOP_TABLE\n- MULTISTOP_IMPACT\n- TUNING_RECOMMENDATIONS\n- CONCISE_NARRATIVE\n\n==================================================\nMULTI-INTENT DOMINANCE RULE (MANDATORY)\n==================================================\nIf the user explicitly requests MORE THAN ONE of:\n  - SUMMARY\n  - FAILURE (root cause / why / infeasible)\n  - MULTISTOP (savings / consolidation)\n  - TUNING (optimize / improve)\n\nThen:\n1. Set primaryMode = SUMMARY\n2. Set modes = list of all requested modes in the order:\n      SUMMARY → FAILURE → MULTISTOP → TUNING\n3. diagnosticViewFlow must include the union of all required views,\n   ordered by the global view order.\n\n==================================================\nPLANNING RULES\n==================================================\n\nANSWER TYPE PRECEDENCE RULE (CRITICAL)\n\n1. First decide answerType (QA vs REPORT).\n2. Then decide modes and diagnosticViewFlow.\n3. answerType MUST NOT be overridden by primaryMode.\n\nIf the user query is a direct question, enumeration, or explanation request\n(e.g., starts with or semantically matches: what, why, how, list, show, which, did, does, is, are, explain),\nTHEN:\n\nanswerType = \"QA\"\n\nUNLESS the user explicitly uses any of these words:\n  \"report\", \"full report\", \"detailed report\", \"summary report\",\n  \"analysis\", \"root cause analysis\", \"diagnostic report\",\n  \"table\", \"breakdown\", \"overview document\"\n\nIn those explicit cases:\nanswerType = \"REPORT\"\n\nThis rule has absolute priority over:\n- primaryMode\n- modes\n- diagnosticViewFlow\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nQA VS REPORT DISAMBIGUATION FOR FAILURE QUERIES\n\nIf the query is of the form:\n- \"List the failed orders\"\n- \"Which orders failed\"\n- \"Why did order X fail\"\n- \"Explain why these orders failed\"\n\nThen:\nanswerType = \"QA\"\nEven though primaryMode = FAILURE.\n\nRender:\n- Entity-level or process-level causal explanation\n- NOT full Bulk Plan Failure Report\n- NOT numbered report sections\n- NOT ASCII trees unless explicitly requested\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDOMAIN GUARD (MANDATORY FIRST STEP)\n\n1. If the query is primarily about:\n- Weather, time, greetings, general knowledge, language translation,\n- Math, programming, or any non-OTM topic\n\nThen:\nisOutOfScope = true  \nprimaryMode = null  \nmodes = []  \nfocus = []  \nentityQuery = null  \ndiagnosticViewFlow = []  \nAll dataNeeds = false \n\n2. If the query asks only for counts, totals, or numbers AND all requested metrics pass the SUMMARY METRICS ELIGIBILITY CHECK:\n   → primaryMode = METRICS_ONLY\n   → diagnosticViewFlow = [\"SUMMARY_METRICS\"]\n   → needSummaryMetrics = true\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nFOLLOW-UP CONTEXT HANDLING (MANDATORY)\n\nThe variable `isFollowUp` is provided by an upstream Context Resolver.\n\nIf isFollowUp = true, then:\n1. diagnosticLogFileId MUST be inherited from:\n     conversationState.lastDiagnosticLogFileId\n\n2. Unless the user explicitly mentions a NEW bulk plan or diagnostic log id,\n   you MUST NOT attempt to re-resolve or change the run context.\n\n3. primaryMode inheritance:\n   - If the user explicitly requests a different analysis type\n     (e.g., “now show multistop savings”, “give tuning suggestions”),\n     override primaryMode.\n   - Otherwise:\n       primaryMode = conversationState.lastPrimaryMode\n\n4. focus inheritance:\n   - If the user explicitly mentions an entity (order, rate, location, equipment),\n     set focus = [\"ENTITY\"] and extract entityQuery.\n   - If the user explicitly mentions a process (processType),\n     set focus = [\"PROCESS\"] and extract processQuery.\n   - Otherwise:\n       focus = conversationState.lastFocus\n\n5. modes inheritance:\n   - If the user explicitly adds or removes analytical goals,\n     recompute modes normally.\n   - Otherwise:\n       modes = conversationState.lastModes\n\n6. dataNeeds recomputation:\n   - Always recompute dataNeeds from the *final* (possibly inherited) modes & focus.\n   - Never reuse previous dataNeeds blindly.\n\n7. The output JSON MUST contain:\n   \"isFollowUp\": true,\n   \"inheritedContext\": {\n       \"diagnosticLogFileId\": conversationState.lastDiagnosticLogFileId,\n       \"previousPrimaryMode\": conversationState.lastPrimaryMode,\n       \"previousFocus\": conversationState.lastFocus\n   }\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nENTITY ENUMERATION RULE\n\nIf the user query:\n- asks to list / show / enumerate entities\n- AND refers to a plural entity type (orders, locations, shipments, equipment)\n- AND does NOT specify a concrete entity GID\n\nThen:\n- Treat this as ENTITY enumeration, NOT scoped entity analysis\n- Do NOT require validation against diagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects\n- Set:\n    focus = [\"ENTITY\"]\n    diagnosticViewFlow = [\"ENTITY_IMPACT\"]\n    needEntityIndex = true\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nENTITY DETECTION AND VALIDATION (MANDATORY)\n\nAn entityQuery MUST be created ONLY if ALL of the following are true:\n\n1) The user provides a concrete OTM GID (e.g. LNMDEMO.BWI_READING_01, R12345, EQP_01).\n2) The GID can be mapped to a business object type via:\n   a) Explicit keywords in the query (Order, Rate, Location, Equipment, Lane), OR\n   b) Membership in diagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects.\n\nEntity types and their validation sources:\n\n- ORDER_RELEASE  → diagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects.ORDER_RELEASE\n- RATE_OFFERING  → diagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects.RATE_OFFERING\n- LOCATION       → diagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects.LOCATION\n- EQUIPMENT      → diagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects.EQUIPMENT\n- LANE           → diagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects.LANE\n\nValidation Rule:\n\nIf a candidate GID is NOT found in the corresponding\ndiagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects list for that entity type:\n\n- Do NOT set entityQuery\n- Do NOT set focus = ENTITY\n- Treat the query as a general SUMMARY / FAILURE / METRICS_ONLY request\n- Add to reason: \"Provided identifier is not present in diagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects for this Bulk Plan run.\"\n\nEntityQuery Construction:\n\nIf validation succeeds, output:\n\n\"entityQuery\": {\n  \"type\": \"<ORDER_RELEASE | RATE_OFFERING | LOCATION | EQUIPMENT | LANE>\",\n  \"value\": \"<validated GID>\"\n}\n\nExamples:\n\nQuery:\n\"How many orders selected for LNMDEMO.20260116-0001_328715\"\n→ No entityQuery (class-level metric, no GID instance)\n\nQuery:\n\"Why did Order LNMDEMO.BWI_READING_01 fail?\"\nAND LNMDEMO.BWI_READING_01 ∈ diagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects.ORDER_RELEASE\n→ entityQuery = { type: ORDER_RELEASE, value: LNMDEMO.BWI_READING_01 }\n\nQuery:\n\"Why did Order ABC123 fail?\"\nAND ABC123 ∉ diagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects.ORDER_RELEASE\n→ No entityQuery (invalid entity for this run)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPROCESS DETECTION AND VALIDATION (MANDATORY)\n\nA processQuery MUST be created ONLY if:\n\n1) The user explicitly mentions a workflow step, stage, or process name\n   (e.g., \"Rate Network Routing Leg\", \"Evaluate Rate Service\", \"Construct Routing Network\").\n\n2) The mentioned process can be mapped to a valid processType in:\n   diagnosticTreeStats.filterObjects.allProcesses\n\nMapping rules:\n- Perform case-insensitive and whitespace-normalized match.\n- Allow partial match only if it uniquely resolves to one processType.\n- If multiple matches exist, do NOT resolve; treat as ambiguous.\n- If no match exists, processQuery MUST be null.\n\nIf validation succeeds, output:\n\n\"processQuery\": {\n  \"processType\": \"<validated processType from allProcesses>\"\n}\n\nIf validation fails:\n- processQuery = null\n- Do NOT add focus = PROCESS\n- Do NOT add PROCESS_IMPACT\n- Add to reason: \"Mentioned process does not match any known processType in this Bulk Plan run.\"\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCONCISE NARRATIVE OVERRIDE (TOP PRIORITY)\n\nIf the user query:\n- asks for explanation or understanding\n- AND does NOT explicitly ask for:\n    summary, report, table, metrics, counts, breakdown, analysis\n\nTHEN:\n- diagnosticViewFlow = [\"CONCISE_NARRATIVE\"]\n- primaryMode is inferred normally (FAILURE / ENTITY / PROCESS / MULTISTOP)\n- modes may still include FAILURE / MULTISTOP for tracking\n- STOP further view planning\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nANSWER TYPE DETERMINATION (MANDATORY)\n\nThe planner must decide whether the user wants:\n\nA) A structured diagnostic REPORT (tables, trees, sections, analysis blocks), OR  \nB) A direct QUESTION–ANSWER (natural language, scoped to the specific question).\n\nSet:\n\nanswerType = \"QA\"\nIF the user query is:\n- A direct question (what, why, how, which, list, show, does, did, is, are)\n- AND does NOT explicitly ask for:\n    report, summary, overview, analysis, breakdown, table, full details, metrics report\n- AND is not requesting a formatted diagnostic artifact\n\nExamples → answerType = \"QA\":\n- \"Did any order fail in this run?\"\n- \"Which orders failed?\"\n- \"Why did order X fail?\"\n- \"What is the total cost?\"\n- \"Is multistop used here?\"\n- \"Explain in simple terms what went wrong\"\n\nSet:\n\nanswerType = \"REPORT\"\nONLY IF the user explicitly requests:\n- summary / full summary\n- report\n- analysis\n- root cause analysis\n- diagnostic breakdown\n- metrics table\n- multistop table\n- tuning recommendations\n\nDefault:\nanswerType = \"QA\"\nunless the wording clearly requests a report-style output.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1. METRICS ONLY\n\nIf the query asks only for numeric counts or totals:\n→ primaryMode = METRICS_ONLY\n→ diagnosticViewFlow = [\"SUMMARY_METRICS\"]\n→ needSummaryMetrics = true\n→ No ENTITY unless a concrete GID is present\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n2. CONCISE NARRATIVE RULE\n\nIf the user query is primarily explanatory in nature and does NOT request\ntables, metrics, reports, or breakdowns, then:\n\n- diagnosticViewFlow = [\"CONCISE_NARRATIVE\"]\n- primaryMode = inferred as usual (FAILURE / ENTITY / PROCESS / MULTISTOP)\n- dataNeeds remain unchanged (reuse existing data logic)\n- Do NOT include any other views\n\nExplanatory intent includes phrases like:\n- why\n- explain\n- what caused\n- what went wrong\n- what does this mean\n- in simple terms\n- briefly explain\n\nExplicitly exclude CONCISE_NARRATIVE if the user asks for:\n- summary\n- report\n- metrics\n- counts\n- table\n- breakdown\n- analyze\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n3. SUMMARY\n\nIf the query asks for summary, overview, or status:\n→ primaryMode = SUMMARY\n→ diagnosticViewFlow = [\"SUMMARY_METRICS\", \"BULK_PLAN_OVERVIEW\"]\n→ needSummaryMetrics = true\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n4. FAILURE\n\nIf the query asks why, failed, infeasible, root cause, bottleneck, dominant constraint:\n→ include FAILURE\n→ diagnosticViewFlow includes:\n   - FAILURE_TREE\n   - DOMINANT_FAILURE\n→ needFailureTree = true\n→ If dominant path or causal cut is requested:\n   → needDominantFailurePaths = true\n→ If audienceLevel = DEVELOPER:\n   → add CONSTRAINT_EVIDENCE\n\nIf entityQuery is present:\n→ Do NOT include SUMMARY_METRICS or BULK_PLAN_OVERVIEW\n→ diagnosticViewFlow = [\"FAILURE_TREE\", \"DOMINANT_FAILURE\", \"ENTITY_IMPACT\"]\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n5. ENTITY FOCUS\nIf EntityQuery is present:\nAdd focus = [\"ENTITY\"] and ENTITY_IMPACT only when entityQuery exists.\nSet needEntityIndex = true.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n6. PROCESS FOCUS\n\nIf processQuery is present:\n- Add focus = [\"PROCESS\"]\n- Include PROCESS_IMPACT in diagnosticViewFlow\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n7. MULTISTOP\n\nIf multistop / consolidation / savings iterations are mentioned:\n→ primaryMode = MULTISTOP\n→ diagnosticViewFlow = [\"MULTISTOP_TABLE\", \"MULTISTOP_IMPACT\"]\n→ needMultistopData = true\n→ Do NOT add SUMMARY unless explicitly requested.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n8. TUNING\n\nIf optimization / tuning / performance is asked:\n→ primaryMode = TUNING\n→ diagnosticViewFlow = [\"TUNING_RECOMMENDATIONS\"]\n→ needTuningGuide = true\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n9. primaryMode is the dominant analytical goal.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n10. View order must follow:\n\nSUMMARY_METRICS →\nBULK_PLAN_OVERVIEW →\nFAILURE_TREE →\nDOMINANT_FAILURE →\nCONSTRAINT_EVIDENCE →\nENTITY_IMPACT →\nPROCESS_IMPACT →\nMULTISTOP_TABLE →\nMULTISTOP_IMPACT →\nTUNING_RECOMMENDATIONS →\nCONCISE_NARRATIVE →\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n11. DATA DEPENDENCY (MANDATORY)\n\nIf needDominantFailurePaths = true  \nThen needFailureTree MUST be true.\n\nNever output:\nneedDominantFailurePaths = true  \nneedFailureTree = false\n\n12. Guardrail (MANDATORY)\n\nIf diagnosticViewFlow contains CONCISE_NARRATIVE, it MUST be the only view in the list.\n\n==================================================\nSUMMARY METRICS ELIGIBILITY CHECK (MANDATORY):\n==================================================\n\nBefore assigning primaryMode = METRICS_ONLY, you MUST verify that the\nuser’s requested metric(s) are fully answerable using ONLY the fields\navailable in SummaryMetrics from diagnosticTreeStats.\n\nSummaryMetrics typically includes execution-level counts such as:\n- totalOrdersSelected\n- totalOrdersPlanned\n- totalOrdersFailed\n- totalShipmentsCreated\n- totalMultistopShipments\n- list of entities like ORDER_RELEASE, EQUIPMENT_GROUP and so on\n\nIf the user asks for any metric NOT present or derivable from SummaryMetrics\n(e.g. total cost, cost savings, distance, utilization, rate amounts,\nfinancial totals, performance tuning impact, etc.):\n\nTHEN:\n- You MUST NOT choose primaryMode = METRICS_ONLY\n- You MUST escalate to an appropriate analytical mode such as:\n  SUMMARY, MULTISTOP, FAILURE, or TUNING\n- And include the corresponding views and dataNeeds flags\n\n==================================================\nQA RENDERING CONTRACT (DOWNSTREAM)\n==================================================\n\nIf answerType = \"QA\":\n\n1. The renderer MUST answer the user's question directly.\n2. Do NOT force report formats, numbered sections, or tables.\n3. Use the same semanticModel and dataNeeds, but:\n   - Select only the minimal data needed to answer the question.\n   - Respect entityQuery / processQuery if present.\n4. Use natural language, deterministic, factual.\n5. If the question is:\n   - Enumerative: return lists.\n   - Yes/No: answer yes/no with short justification.\n   - Why: explain using dominant failure or process cut.\n   - What: extract directly from summaryMetrics / entityImpact / failureTreeData.\n6. No Bulk Plan Summary format unless answerType = REPORT.\n\n==================================================\nUSER QUERY\n==================================================\n{{$context.$variables.userQuery}}\n\nReturn STRICT JSON only.\nNo markdown.\nNo commentary.\nNo extra text."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"OTM Bulk Plan Diagnostic Intent Plan\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\n    \"isOutOfScope\",\n    \"answerType\",\n    \"primaryMode\",\n    \"modes\",\n    \"focus\",\n    \"audienceLevel\",\n    \"diagnosticViewFlow\",\n    \"dataNeeds\",\n    \"reason\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"isOutOfScope\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"True if the query is not related to OTM Bulk Plan diagnostics\"\n    },\n    \"answerType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"REPORT\", \"QA\"]\n    },\n    \"primaryMode\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n      \"enum\": [\"SUMMARY\", \"METRICS_ONLY\", \"FAILURE\", \"MULTISTOP\", \"TUNING\", null]\n    },\n    \"modes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"enum\": [\"SUMMARY\", \"METRICS_ONLY\", \"FAILURE\", \"MULTISTOP\", \"TUNING\"]\n      }\n    },\n    \"focus\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"enum\": [\"ENTITY\", \"PROCESS\"]\n      }\n    },\n    \"entityQuery\": {\n      \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"],\n      \"required\": [\"type\", \"value\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"type\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n        },\n        \"value\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"processQuery\": {\n      \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"],\n      \"required\": [\"processType\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"processType\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"audienceLevel\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"USER\", \"PLANNER\", \"DEVELOPER\"]\n    },\n    \"diagnosticViewFlow\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"enum\": [\n          \"SUMMARY_METRICS\",\n          \"BULK_PLAN_OVERVIEW\",\n          \"FAILURE_TREE\",\n          \"DOMINANT_FAILURE\",\n          \"CONSTRAINT_EVIDENCE\",\n          \"ENTITY_IMPACT\",\n          \"PROCESS_IMPACT\",\n          \"MULTISTOP_TABLE\",\n          \"MULTISTOP_IMPACT\",\n          \"TUNING_RECOMMENDATIONS\",\n          \"CONCISE_NARRATIVE\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"dataNeeds\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\n        \"needSummaryMetrics\",\n        \"needFailureTree\",\n        \"needDominantFailurePaths\",\n        \"needEntityIndex\",\n        \"needMultistopData\",\n        \"needTuningGuide\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"needSummaryMetrics\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n        \"needFailureTree\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n        \"needDominantFailurePaths\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n        \"needEntityIndex\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n        \"needMultistopData\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n        \"needTuningGuide\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" }\n      },\n      \"allOf\": [\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"needDominantFailurePaths\": { \"const\": true }\n            }\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"needFailureTree\": { \"const\": true }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"isFollowUp\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"True if the query is a follow up query\"\n    },\n    \"inheritedContext\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\n        \"diagnosticLogFileId\",\n        \"previousPrimaryMode\",\n        \"previousFocus\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"diagnosticLogFileId\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"nullable\": true\n        },\n        \"previousPrimaryMode\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"nullable\": true,\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"SUMMARY\",\n            \"FAILURE\",\n            \"MULTISTOP\",\n            \"TUNING\",\n            \"METRICS_ONLY\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"previousFocus\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\"ENTITY\", \"PROCESS\"]\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"reason\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
